Nethack With Tiles 1.3.0 has been released.
http://www.darkarts.co.za/projects/newt/

Summary of changes:
 - Use tab to switch between ascii mode and tiles
 - visible infra red and telepathic vision indicators
 - translucent tilesets now display in inventory
 - all window fonts now dynamic and setable in game config
 - Windows is now a supported platform
 - Slash'EM upgraded to 0.0.7E7F2
 - Several minor bug fixes and tweaks

About:
NEthack With Tiles is my attempt to recreate the standard NetHack and
Slash'EM tty interface, but with tiles additionally to standard console
text. Newt's interface is identical to that of the tty/console
interface in layout, in behaviour and even in the way messages and any
other text are displayed. The only difference being that you now have
an ingame/runtime toggle key switching between text and tiles.

Newt supports:
 - All known 2D flat tilesets.
 - Joystick support (yes, I added this at a whim for my own
   amusement, as far as I am aware, this is the only NetHack
   interface that is playable with the joystick).
 - Windowed or fullscreen gameplay at the resolution of your choice.
 - Auto fit map into game window horizontally,vertically or both
   (by keeping aspect)
 - Zoom in and out

